1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,191
G20 Tech turns drone imagery into decisions.

2
00:00:03,241 --> 00:00:05,450
Follow one survey, start to finish.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:10,357
Each organization gets its own workspace: projects, tasks and their status.

4
00:00:10,407 --> 00:00:15,333
Flights are stored as reusable datasets: upload once, process as often as needed.

5
00:00:15,683 --> 00:00:22,387
This dataset is a single flight: sixty-eight photos, each carrying its GPS position and capture time.

6
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:28,956
Processing runs on the OpenDroneMap engine, managed from the browser.

7
00:00:29,006 --> 00:00:36,188
This task turned those photos into a five-centimetre orthophoto, elevation models, a point cloud and a 3D model.

8
00:00:36,238 --> 00:00:38,900
A new task needs only images and a preset.

9
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:46,120
Open the task and the orthophoto is on the map, with each camera position and the flight path.

10
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:53,262
Switch the basemap for context, then zoom from the whole site down to five centimetres per pixel.

11
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,621
Elevation comes too.

12
00:00:56,671 --> 00:01:03,576
The surface model shows buildings and trees; blend it over the imagery, or switch to bare-earth terrain.

13
00:01:06,383 --> 00:01:08,384
Measurement happens on the map.

14
00:01:08,434 --> 00:01:15,395
Outline a building and the platform returns its footprint and its volume, computed from the surface model.

15
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:20,453
The same survey as a textured 3D model.

16
00:01:20,503 --> 00:01:26,829
Rotate it, zoom in, pan across it, right in the browser, with nothing to install.

17
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:37,606
For full detail there is the point cloud: ten million points, streamed as you move.

18
00:01:37,656 --> 00:01:42,293
Colour it by elevation, or by class: ground, vegetation, buildings.

19
00:01:42,343 --> 00:01:46,631
Draw a line across the site and read off an elevation profile.

20
00:01:53,683 --> 00:01:56,560
Analysis plugins bring AI to every survey.

21
00:01:56,610 --> 00:01:59,417
Here, a detector for vehicles and people.

22
00:01:59,767 --> 00:02:10,317
The result comes back as map data: one hundred and eighty-four objects on this site, each with a class and a confidence score, ready to download.

23
00:02:12,217 --> 00:02:19,644
Change detection compares two surveys of one site and reports cut and fill volumes with their uncertainty.

24
00:02:19,694 --> 00:02:27,333
In this demo both inputs are runs of the same flight, so it finds almost nothing: half a percent of the site.

25
00:02:27,683 --> 00:02:34,772
Results leave the platform in standard formats: cloud-optimized GeoTIFFs, a LAZ point cloud and a GLB model.

26
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:36,901
The analysis layer is open.

27
00:02:36,951 --> 00:02:45,050
Plugins are enabled per organization and distributed through a built-in marketplace, so new models arrive without changing the platform.

28
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,656
Drone data, processing, visualization, AI analysis, insight.

29
00:02:48,706 --> 00:02:50,750
One platform, from flight to decision.
